; Wildcard DNS Zone File for Testing
; Demonstrates wildcard matching behavior, precedence rules, and exception handling
; Tests domain matching module (dns/domain from domain.c and domain-match.c)
; Validates RFC 4592 compliance for wildcard DNS records
;
; Domain: wildcard.test
; Purpose: Integration testing of wildcard resolution logic
;
; RFC 4592 Wildcard Rules Tested:
; 1. Wildcards only match when there's no exact match
; 2. Specific records always take precedence over wildcards
; 3. Empty non-terminals block wildcard matching
; 4. Wildcards apply to the immediate child label only
;

$TTL 3600
$ORIGIN wildcard.test.

; Standard zone authority records
@       SOA     ns1.wildcard.test. admin.wildcard.test. (
                2024010601      ; Serial (YYYYMMDDNN format)
                7200            ; Refresh (2 hours)
                3600            ; Retry (1 hour)
                1209600         ; Expire (2 weeks)
                86400 )         ; Minimum TTL (1 day)

; Nameservers
@       NS      ns1.wildcard.test.
@       NS      ns2.wildcard.test.

ns1     A       192.0.2.1
ns2     A       192.0.2.2

;
; SECTION 1: Basic Wildcard Records
; Tests simple wildcard matching at the zone apex level
;

; Wildcard A record - matches any subdomain not explicitly defined
*.wildcard.test.        A       192.0.2.100

; Wildcard AAAA record - matches any subdomain for IPv6
*.wildcard.test.        AAAA    2001:db8::100

; Wildcard MX record - provides mail exchanger for any subdomain
*.wildcard.test.        MX      10 mail.wildcard.test.

; Wildcard TXT record - informational text for any subdomain
*.wildcard.test.        TXT     "Wildcard TXT record for any subdomain"

;
; SECTION 2: Specific Records Override Wildcards (RFC 4592 Section 2.2.1)
; Tests precedence where explicit records take priority over wildcards
;

; Explicit record for www - overrides wildcard *.wildcard.test
www.wildcard.test.      A       192.0.2.10
www.wildcard.test.      AAAA    2001:db8::10
www.wildcard.test.      TXT     "Explicit www record, NOT wildcard"

; Explicit record for mail - overrides wildcard *.wildcard.test
mail.wildcard.test.     A       192.0.2.20
mail.wildcard.test.     AAAA    2001:db8::20
mail.wildcard.test.     MX      10 mail.wildcard.test.
mail.wildcard.test.     TXT     "Explicit mail server"

; Explicit record for ftp - overrides wildcard *.wildcard.test
ftp.wildcard.test.      A       192.0.2.30
ftp.wildcard.test.      TXT     "Explicit FTP server"

;
; SECTION 3: Multiple Wildcard Levels
; Tests wildcards at different delegation levels
;

; Second-level wildcard for subdomain
*.sub.wildcard.test.    A       192.0.2.200
*.sub.wildcard.test.    AAAA    2001:db8::200
*.sub.wildcard.test.    TXT     "Wildcard for *.sub.wildcard.test"

; Specific override within sub.wildcard.test
www.sub.wildcard.test.  A       192.0.2.210
www.sub.wildcard.test.  TXT     "Explicit www.sub, overrides *.sub wildcard"

; Third-level wildcard
*.deep.sub.wildcard.test.       A       192.0.2.300
*.deep.sub.wildcard.test.       TXT     "Third-level wildcard"

;
; SECTION 4: Wildcard with CNAME Records
; Tests CNAME behavior with wildcards
;

; Wildcard CNAME - any subdomain under alias points to target
*.alias.wildcard.test.  CNAME   target.wildcard.test.
target.wildcard.test.   A       192.0.2.50
target.wildcard.test.   AAAA    2001:db8::50

;
; SECTION 5: Empty Non-Terminals (RFC 4592 Section 2.2.2)
; Tests wildcard blocking by intermediate labels
;

; Empty non-terminal: creates intermediate.wildcard.test without records
; This blocks *.wildcard.test from matching hosts.intermediate.wildcard.test
intermediate.wildcard.test.     NS      ns.intermediate.wildcard.test.

; Glue record for the NS delegation
ns.intermediate.wildcard.test.  A       192.0.2.60

; Explicit record deeper in the tree
host.intermediate.wildcard.test.        A       192.0.2.61
host.intermediate.wildcard.test.        TXT     "Explicit host under empty non-terminal"

; Note: Queries for random.intermediate.wildcard.test will return NXDOMAIN
; because 'intermediate' is an empty non-terminal that blocks wildcard matching

;
; SECTION 6: Multiple Record Types on Same Wildcard
; Tests comprehensive record type coverage for wildcard domains
;

*.multi.wildcard.test.  A       192.0.2.150
*.multi.wildcard.test.  A       192.0.2.151
*.multi.wildcard.test.  AAAA    2001:db8::150
*.multi.wildcard.test.  AAAA    2001:db8::151
*.multi.wildcard.test.  MX      10 mail1.wildcard.test.
*.multi.wildcard.test.  MX      20 mail2.wildcard.test.
*.multi.wildcard.test.  TXT     "Multiple record types"
*.multi.wildcard.test.  TXT     "Second TXT record"

;
; SECTION 7: Wildcard Matching Edge Cases
;

; Wildcard at different TTLs to test TTL handling
*.ttl.wildcard.test.    300     A       192.0.2.250
*.ttl.wildcard.test.    600     AAAA    2001:db8::250

; Wildcard for testing case-insensitive matching
*.CaSe.wildcard.test.   A       192.0.2.251
*.CaSe.wildcard.test.   TXT     "Case-insensitive test"

;
; SECTION 8: Wildcard with Internationalized Labels
; Tests wildcard behavior with non-ASCII labels (if IDN support is enabled)
;

; Example with punycode for internationalized domain names
*.xn--example-9ua.wildcard.test.        A       192.0.2.252
*.xn--example-9ua.wildcard.test.        TXT     "IDN wildcard (xn--example-9ua = exämple)"

;
; SECTION 9: Wildcard Precedence Test Cases
; Explicit scenarios for testing precedence logic
;

; Scenario A: Wildcard exists, no specific record
; Query: anything.wildcard.test -> Should return 192.0.2.100 (from *.wildcard.test)

; Scenario B: Wildcard exists, specific record exists
; Query: www.wildcard.test -> Should return 192.0.2.10 (specific record)

; Scenario C: Nested wildcard, no specific record
; Query: anything.sub.wildcard.test -> Should return 192.0.2.200 (from *.sub.wildcard.test)

; Scenario D: Nested wildcard, specific record exists
; Query: www.sub.wildcard.test -> Should return 192.0.2.210 (specific record)

; Scenario E: Empty non-terminal blocks wildcard
; Query: random.intermediate.wildcard.test -> Should return NXDOMAIN

; Scenario F: Triple-level query
; Query: random.deep.sub.wildcard.test -> Should return 192.0.2.300

; Scenario G: Wildcard CNAME resolution
; Query: random.alias.wildcard.test -> Should CNAME to target.wildcard.test, then return 192.0.2.50

;
; SECTION 10: Negative Testing - No Wildcard Match
;

; Explicit record with no wildcard at this level
explicit-only.wildcard.test.    A       192.0.2.253
explicit-only.wildcard.test.    TXT     "No wildcard at this level"

; Query: anything.explicit-only.wildcard.test -> Should return NXDOMAIN
; (No wildcard *.explicit-only.wildcard.test defined)

;
; SECTION 11: RFC 4592 Compliance Examples
;

; Example from RFC 4592 Section 2.1.1
; Demonstrates closest encloser and source of synthesis
*.example.wildcard.test.        A       192.0.2.254
*.example.wildcard.test.        MX      10 mail.wildcard.test.

host1.example.wildcard.test.    A       192.0.2.240
host1.example.wildcard.test.    TXT     "Explicit host1"

; Query: host2.example.wildcard.test -> Synthesized from *.example.wildcard.test
; Query: host1.example.wildcard.test -> Returns explicit record 192.0.2.240

;
; SECTION 12: Wildcard with Different Classes (Future Extension)
; Standard zone files typically only use IN (Internet) class
;

*.class-test.wildcard.test.     IN      A       192.0.2.255
*.class-test.wildcard.test.     IN      TXT     "Internet class wildcard"

;
; END OF WILDCARD ZONE FILE
;
; Test Coverage Summary:
; - Basic wildcard records (A, AAAA, MX, TXT, CNAME)
; - Specific record precedence over wildcards
; - Multiple wildcard levels (2nd and 3rd level)
; - Empty non-terminal blocking
; - Multiple record types on same wildcard
; - TTL variations
; - Case-insensitive matching
; - IDN/Punycode wildcards
; - RFC 4592 compliance scenarios
; - Negative test cases (NXDOMAIN expectations)
;
; Expected Behavior for Rust Implementation:
; 1. dns/domain module must implement wildcard matching per RFC 4592
; 2. Specific records must always take precedence over wildcards
; 3. Empty non-terminals must block wildcard expansion
; 4. Wildcard synthesis must generate appropriate responses
; 5. Case-insensitive domain matching must be preserved
; 6. CNAME wildcards must follow CNAME chain resolution rules
;
